Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:33:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Backfill production-applied migrations and their SQL suite
 into main

Production has 21 migrations applied from the hosted purge checkpoint
(f058138), 20260905210811 staged_uploads through 20260906051631
project_content_purge, that main's migration directory never carried.
Add them byte-identical; every file's SHA-256 matches the hash recorded
in that checkpoint's operations evidence.

Bring the checkpoint's SQL test files (supabase/tests, tests/sql) and its
run-local.sh steps, three-way merged with the guarded-publication tests.
main's previous tests/sql/delivery.sql asserted the pre-project_recovery
live_reader_responses signature and fails against the production schema.
The storage-audit vitest bridge is omitted; it exercises apps/edge Worker
tests that ship with the staged-uploads application slice.

Verified: supabase/tests/run-local.sh on disposable PostgreSQL 17 passes
with all 30 migrations, including both guarded-publication proof orders.
No hosted change.

